
<p>Fred Potter, on LinkedIn:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>So if you ever meet someone who tells you, “At Apple, I’m the one
who did this,” take it with a grain of salt. They were probably
part of the team that made it happen, and that’s already something
to be proud of.</p>

<p>Sometimes, when the final product finally comes out, you can
recognize a few of the personal touches you contributed along the
way. And that, in itself, is immensely rewarding.</p>

<p>Wishing HomeView every success!</p>
</blockquote>

<p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/frpotter/">Potter’s LinkedIn bio</a> lists his time at Apple as July 2021 through June 2024, and describes it only as “Worked on HomeView”. (<a href="https://www.igen.fr/domotique/2026/10/homeview-un-modele-motorise-deja-dans-les-cartons-et-une-petite-touche-francaise-158755">Via Christophe Laporte at iGeneration</a>.)</p>

